#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:5
msgid ""
"This is the primary mechanism that makes every prompt smarter. Run `hero "
"resume` (alias: `hero load`) and read the output **before doing anything "
"else** — it contains the focused, ranked subgraph relevant to this "
"session: who you are, what's in flight, what just changed, dead ends to "
"skip, blockers, and files-nearby context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:11
msgid "**When to use:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:13
msgid "At the start of every fresh session in a hero-aware repo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:14
msgid "After a long pause (>1 hour) where state may have moved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:15
msgid "After switching branches or pulling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:16
msgid "Whenever you feel like you're missing context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:17
msgid ""
"Whenever the user says \"resume\", \"pick up\", \"continue\", \"where are"
" we\", \"catch me up\", \"what's going on\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:20
msgid "**Steps:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:22
msgid ""
"Run `hero resume` (or `hero resume --auto` to bias scoring toward "
"currently-changed files)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:24
msgid ""
"Read the entire output. Do not summarize it back to the user — it's for "
"you, the agent. Treat it as system context for everything that follows in"
" this session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:27
msgid ""
"If a section ends with `_…+N more — hero search <topic> to dig deeper_`, "
"that's a relief valve. When the user asks something that touches that "
"area, run `hero search <topic>` to pull more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:30
msgid ""
"If you need to understand WHY something is where it is, run `hero why "
"<slug>` to traverse the graph backwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:32
msgid ""
"If the user asks \"what's blocked?\" or \"what should I work on?\", "
"prefer the resume output's `Blocked on` and `In flight` sections over re-"
"deriving from scratch by reading files. For a paste-ready list of ready-"
"to-pick-up specs (each with a kickoff prompt), call `hero_queue` via MCP "
"or read `.hero/QUEUE.md` directly. The queue is the cold-start surface; "
"resume is the warm-context surface — they compose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:39
msgid ""
"The first item in `In flight` is usually the right next action. Propose "
"it directly — don't ask \"what should we work on?\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:42
msgid "**Why this matters:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:44
msgid ""
"Hero captures every commit, spec, decision, attempt, and cross-repo "
"dependency over the project's life. The resume output is the digest — "
"bounded, ranked, fresh — that puts the most-relevant slice into your "
"context window so the user gets a hot session even on a cold box. Without"
" it, you're doing the work the digester already did, slower and less "
"accurately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:51
msgid "**If `hero resume` fails or returns nothing:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:53
msgid ""
"The graph may not be populated yet. Run `hero scan` (or `hero graph "
"reingest all`) to populate it from the local sources of truth (code, "
"specs, git log, NEXT.md). Then re-run `hero resume`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:57
msgid ""
"**What to say** (natural-language triggers — agents should auto-route "
"these to `/resume` without the user having to know the command name):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:60
msgid ""
"\"resume\", \"let's resume\", \"let's continue\", \"continue\", \"pick up"
" where we left off\", \"where are we\", \"what's going on\", \"catch me "
"up\", \"load context\", \"load up\", \"load me up\", \"starting fresh\", "
"\"fresh session\", \"hot session\", \"warm me up\", \"what should I work "
"on\", \"what's the status\", \"give me the lay of the land\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/resume.md:66
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Also: at the start of any new session in this repo, before responding to "
"the user's first substantive message, run `hero resume` unconditionally. "
"It's ≥99% useful and never wrong — it costs nothing to fire, and it "
"prevents the agent from re-deriving context the graph already has."
msgstr ""

